# Files in this repo that are NOT part of the published site.
#
# This is the Cloudflare half of what `_redirects` used to do. Netlify could
# only hide a repo file with a forced 404 rule (`404!`) because a deploy from
# the repository root uploads everything; Cloudflare's `_redirects` has no 404
# status, and the stronger equivalent is not uploading the file at all. A path
# that was never deployed cannot be served by mistake.
#
# `tools/audit.mjs` (check 16) asserts the pair stays complete: every tracked
# file is either intentionally public or listed here, and every pattern here
# matches something real — an ignore rule that matches nothing is a rule that
# would have silently stopped being true the day the file it was meant for
# returned. The tool-state patterns below are exempt from that second half:
# they may not exist on a fresh clone.

# Repository and tooling. The assets layer does not exclude dot-entries by
# itself, so every one at the publish root is listed here.
.git/
.github/
.assetsignore
.gitignore

# Local tool state and OS noise — may not exist on a fresh clone; listed so
# that when they do exist they are never uploaded.
.wrangler/
.netlify/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

netlify/
tools/

README.md
netlify.toml
_headers
wrangler.toml
worker.js
